  "verseCount": 21,
  "content": [
    {
      "name": "chapter",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "number": "12",
        "style": "c",
        "sid": "2KI 12"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "12",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "s1"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Joash Repairs the Temple",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.12.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.12.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 12:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In the seventh year of Jehu, Joash",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.12.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.12.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "became king, and he reigned in Jerusalem forty years. His mother's name was Zibiah; she was from Beersheba.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.12.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.12.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 12:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Joash did what was right in the eyes of the",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.12.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.12.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "char",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "nd"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Lord",
              "type": "text",
              "attrs": {
                "verseId": "2KI.12.2",
                "verseOrgIds": [
                  "2KI.12.3"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "all the years Jehoiada the priest instructed him.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.12.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.12.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 12:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The high places, however, were not removed; the people continued to offer sacrifices and burn incense there.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.12.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.12.4"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 12:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Joash said to the priests, \"Collect all the money that is brought as sacred offerings to the temple of the",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.12.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.12.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "char",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "nd"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Lord",
              "type": "text",
              "attrs": {
                "verseId": "2KI.12.4",
                "verseOrgIds": [
                  "2KI.12.5"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "—the money collected in the census, the money received from personal vows and the money brought voluntarily to the temple.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.12.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.12.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 12:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Let every priest receive the money from one of the treasurers, then use it to repair whatever damage is found in the temple.\"",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.12.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.12.6"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 12:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But by the twenty-third year of King Joash the priests still had not repaired the temple.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.12.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.12.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 12:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Therefore King Joash summoned Jehoiada the priest and the other priests and asked them, \"Why aren't you repairing the damage done to the temple? Take no more money from your treasurers, but hand it over for repairing the temple.\"",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.12.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.12.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 12:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The priests agreed that they would not collect any more money from the people and that they would not repair the temple themselves.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.12.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.12.9"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 12:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Jehoiada the priest took a chest and bored a hole in its lid. He placed it beside the altar, on the right side as one enters the temple of the",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.12.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.12.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "char",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "nd"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Lord",
              "type": "text",
              "attrs": {
                "verseId": "2KI.12.9",
                "verseOrgIds": [
                  "2KI.12.10"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": ". The priests who guarded the entrance put into the chest all the money that was brought to the temple of the",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.12.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.12.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "char",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "nd"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Lord",
              "type": "text",
              "attrs": {
                "verseId": "2KI.12.9",
                "verseOrgIds": [
                  "2KI.12.10"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.12.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.12.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 12:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Whenever they saw that there was a large amount of money in the chest, the royal secretary and the high priest came, counted the money that had been brought into the temple of the",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.12.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.12.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "char",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "nd"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Lord",
              "type": "text",
              "attrs": {
                "verseId": "2KI.12.10",
                "verseOrgIds": [
                  "2KI.12.11"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and put it into bags.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.12.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.12.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 12:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "When the amount had been determined, they gave the money to the men appointed to supervise the work on the temple. With it they paid those who worked on the temple of the",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.12.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.12.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "char",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "nd"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Lord",
              "type": "text",
              "attrs": {
                "verseId": "2KI.12.11",
                "verseOrgIds": [
                  "2KI.12.12"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "—the carpenters and builders,",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.12.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.12.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 12:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "the masons and stonecutters. They purchased timber and blocks of dressed stone for the repair of the temple of the",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.12.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.12.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "char",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "nd"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Lord",
              "type": "text",
              "attrs": {
                "verseId": "2KI.12.12",
                "verseOrgIds": [
                  "2KI.12.13"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": ", and met all the other expenses of restoring the temple.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.12.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.12.13"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 12:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The money brought into the temple was not spent for making silver basins, wick trimmers, sprinkling bowls, trumpets or any other articles of gold or silver for the temple of the",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.12.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.12.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "char",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "nd"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Lord",
              "type": "text",
              "attrs": {
                "verseId": "2KI.12.13",
                "verseOrgIds": [
                  "2KI.12.14"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": ";",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.12.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.12.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 12:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "it was paid to the workers, who used it to repair the temple.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.12.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.12.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 12:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "They did not require an accounting from those to whom they gave the money to pay the workers, because they acted with complete honesty.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.12.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.12.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 12:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The money from the guilt offerings and sin offerings",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.12.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.12.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "was not brought into the temple of the",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.12.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.12.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "char",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "nd"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Lord",
              "type": "text",
              "attrs": {
                "verseId": "2KI.12.16",
                "verseOrgIds": [
                  "2KI.12.17"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "; it belonged to the priests.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.12.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.12.17"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 12:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "About this time Hazael king of Aram went up and attacked Gath and captured it. Then he turned to attack Jerusalem.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.12.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.12.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "18",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 12:18"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But Joash king of Judah took all the sacred objects dedicated by his predecessors—Jehoshaphat, Jehoram and Ahaziah, the kings of Judah—and the gifts he himself had dedicated and all the gold found in the treasuries of the temple of the",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.12.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.12.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "char",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "nd"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Lord",
              "type": "text",
              "attrs": {
                "verseId": "2KI.12.18",
                "verseOrgIds": [
                  "2KI.12.19"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and of the royal palace, and he sent them to Hazael king of Aram, who then withdrew from Jerusalem.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.12.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.12.19"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 12:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "As for the other events of the reign of Joash, and all he did, are they not written in the book of the annals of the kings of Judah?",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.12.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.12.20"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "20",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 12:20"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "20",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "His officials conspired against him and assassinated him at Beth Millo, on the road down to Silla.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.12.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.12.21"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "21",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2KI 12:21"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "21",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The officials who murdered him were Jozabad son of Shimeath and Jehozabad son of Shomer. He died and was buried with his ancestors in the City of David. And Amaziah his son succeeded him as king.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2KI.12.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2KI.12.22"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "next": {
    "id": "2KI.13",
    "number": "13",
    "bookId": "2KI"
  },
  "previous": {
    "id": "2KI.11",
    "number": "11",
